10. Conclusion
Campus Event Manager demonstrates how MongoDB can be used to build a practical NoSQL application. The project combines document modeling, embedded arrays, references, validation, indexes, CRUD operations and aggregation pipelines within a Flask application.
The resulting application provides complete management of users, events and registrations while also offering analytical views of event participation.
The project also demonstrates the advantages of MongoDB's flexible document model, particularly for embedded event locations and registration arrays, while maintaining references for reusable user information.